  "notes": "Waiver filing, cash basis, one column per fund. Governmental = General, Street, Improvement funds; business-type = Electric, Water, Sewer, Garbage. Page 1a (Improvement) totals are included in the p1 Total column. Governmental roll: 40,078 + 62,969 - 66,416 + 26,218 - 1,180 = 61,669. Business roll: 158,966 + 112,680 - 90,680 - 25,038 = 155,928. Transfers tie to the Schedule of Interfund Transfers (p5): Electric -> General 25,038, General -> Street 1,180. Debt Service 3,673 sits in the Water Fund column (GO Water Bond) so it is business-type. Utility 'Local Receipts: Other' lines (Electric 79,521, Water 18,943, Sewer 4,430, Garbage 8,306) are assumed to be utility sales and are category Utility Charges (attempt 2, verifier fix 2026-10-28; Electric/Water/Sewer marked review because the form does not say what they are). Receipt/disbursement original_label carries the fund column in parentheses to tell the per-column lines apart; the printed row label is the text before the parentheses. Balance sheet is just the ending balances: no balance statement in filing; investments none (p5). Schedule of Outstanding Debt (p5): GO Water Bond 95,496 outstanding at 9/30/25 (informational; cash-basis statements carry no liabilities, so it is not a balance sheet line). No detail schedules. Read pages 1-5 of 5"
